pycma attribution
=================

`jax_helper.optimization.cmaes` is a derivative work of pycma (the `cma`
package), a pure-Python implementation of the CMA-ES algorithm.  It reproduces
pycma's default isotropic CMA-ES code path, including its arithmetic operation
order, so that for equal normal samples it produces bitwise identical state.

  pycma
  https://github.com/CMA-ES/pycma
  Copyright (c) 2014 Inria
  Author: Nikolaus Hansen, 2008-
  Author: Petr Baudis, 2014
  Author: Youhei Akimoto, 2016-

  Upstream version tracked: cma==4.5.0

pycma is distributed under the BSD 3-Clause License, reproduced verbatim below.
Note that the `cma` package is an independent reference implementation: it is
not a dependency of `jax_helper` and is never imported by the library.  It is a
development dependency only, used to verify that this port matches bitwise.


